/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 716 Tm (Solving a linear equation) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 697 Tm (To solve ax + b = c, undo each step in reverse.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 680 Tm (1. Subtract b from both sides: ax = c - b.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 663 Tm (2. Divide both sides by a: x = \(c - b\) / a.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 646 Tm (3. Put x back into the equation to check it.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 629 Tm (Reading a line) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 610 Tm (Slope-intercept form: y = mx + b. m is the slope, b is where it crosses the y axis.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 593 Tm (Slope = rise over run = \(y2 - y1\) / \(x2 - x1\).) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 576 Tm (Parallel lines have the same slope. Perpendicular lines have slopes that multiply to -1.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 559 Tm (Intercepts) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 540 Tm (The y intercept: set x = 0. The x intercept: set y = 0.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 523 Tm (Mistakes to avoid) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 504 Tm (Do not subtract b from only one side. Whatever you do to one side, do to the other.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 487 Tm (Do not forget the sign: in 5 - 2x = -7, the -2 stays with the x.) Tj
